[ ================================================================ ]
[ 000 -- hello world                                               ]
[                                                                  ]
[     phoenix examples/000_hello_world.phx                         ]
[ ================================================================ ]

[ This is a comment. It runs from the opening bracket to the next  ]
[ closing one.                                                     ]
[                                                                  ]
[ Comments do NOT nest, and there is no way to put a bracket        ]
[ inside one. An unclosed comment swallows the rest of the file,    ]
[ which is by design but worth knowing the first time it happens.   ]

[ Phoenix has no strings. It has one type, the 64 bit float, and    ]
[ two ways to print one:                                            ]
[                                                                   ]
[     print   writes the number itself                              ]
[     printa  writes the character with that ASCII code             ]
[                                                                   ]
[ So text is written one code at a time. 72 is H, 101 is e, and so  ]
[ on; 10 is the newline.                                            ]

72 printa
101 printa
108 printa
108 printa
111 printa
33 printa
10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     Hello!                                                        ]
[                                                                   ]
[ Spelling everything out like this gets old fast. Example 060      ]
[ builds a helper that prints a whole line at once, but it needs    ]
[ loops and functions first.                                        ]
